1
00:00:00,000 --> 00:00:19,000
Ainize.ai: a real public website, not a localhost demo.
First, connect the wallet to sign in.

2
00:00:19,000 --> 00:00:38,000
Official MetaMask: review and sign the Ainize login challenge.
This proves wallet ownership; it is not a transaction or spending approval.

3
00:00:38,000 --> 00:00:47,000
The signed-in account opens Live Test from the site navigation.

4
00:00:47,000 --> 00:01:04,000
The Graph: ask for the USDC contract using fresh indexed Ethereum data.
The model answers from the actual provider result, with its source block.

5
00:01:04,000 --> 00:01:20,000
Inspect the provider data, block and SHA-256 for traceability.
Live source grounding is not memory training or a benchmark accuracy claim.

6
00:01:20,000 --> 00:01:42,000
ENS on Sepolia: resolve patch.ainize-4782c76e.eth and ask about its records.
The same public Live Test calls the real source and model APIs.

7
00:01:42,000 --> 00:02:08,000
The answer identifies the node, knowledge patch and linked Graph dataset.
It preserves the actual REJECTED status; ENS naming does not verify a patch.

8
00:02:08,000 --> 00:02:35,000
The source block and result hash make this lookup inspectable.
No private key, seed phrase or server credential is included in this recording.

9
00:02:35,000 --> 00:03:00,000
Real wallet login, Live Test, Graph answer, then ENS answer.
Source code and recording evidence: github.com/ainblockchain/ainize
